{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537121-summon-familiar","id":1537121,"title":"Summon Familiar","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-06-09T16:42:43-07:00","id":1537121,"title":"Summon Familiar","content":"So, a crow familiar.....<br /> <br /> Spirit 3/Corr 3? And it just uses a charm or whatever to inhabit the crow or...<br /> <br /> I'm trying to figure out what I'd need to explain how I got the familiar on my own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T23:51:03-07:00","id":1537135,"title":"","content":"There are many ways to create a familiar. It can be:<br /> - A robot<br /> - A possesed robot<br /> - A new creature created from scratch<br /> - A mutated existing creature<br /> - A wraith<br /> - A umbral spirit<br /> - A wraith possesing something<br /> - A umbral spirit possesing something<br /> <br /> Or any combination of the above. How you got him depends on the method. In case of a spirit in a crow i would say you only need Spirit 2 to summon it and make a bargain. The spirit will posses the crow on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T03:19:46-07:00","id":1537140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thkaal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537121-summon-familiar#post1537121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, a crow familiar.....<br /> <br /> Spirit 3/Corr 3? And it just uses a charm or whatever to inhabit the crow or...<br /> <br /> I'm trying to figure out what I'd need to explain how I got the familiar on my own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that aside from Possession, the crow Spirit could also utilize the Manifest Charm and doesn't necessarily need a body. There are a few useful perks to ephemeral Familiars.<br /> <br /> Familiars have a way of 'finding' their Mages, more often than the other way around. Sometimes it is as simple as having a crow tap on your window one day.<br /> <br /> If you want to be more active in the process:<br /> <br /> - Your Mage befriended or raised a mundane crow. With Spirit 3 you can wake its Spirit to deepen the relationship and form a Familiar bond.<br /> - Alternatively you could use Life to make the crow sentient enough to accept the Familiar bond.<br /> - You worked with a free crow Spirit often and the Familiar bond was a natural progression. Spirit 2 is sufficient for that.<br /> - If you want to actively look for a Familiar (especially a Spirit), it might be one of the Avatar's past - you could use that connection for divination or scrying to locate it (Correspondence / Time)<br /> - Or use Fate Magick (Entropy) to find your destined Familiar.<br /> <br /> Most Mages will have the means to do at least some of that, so don't worry about stats too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}